> I confess I don't really understand what you're trying to do (correlate occupancy's p to sigma and phi? develop an integrated model?). You might be able to fit something like gdistsamp(~1, ~site, ~1), but if you are predicting that expected values for occupancy/density vary across sites due to habitat/landscape differences, why not just model lambda and phi as varying this way using covariates rather than as a bunch of different intercepts?

